## Quotes of the original text: a word in its verse, a dictionary term or verses word by word (src/kind/original.rs).

cite-option-pronunciation = Pronunciation
cite-option-grammar = Grammar
cite-option-here = Meaning here
cite-option-also = Other meanings
cite-option-senses = Dictionary senses
cite-option-renderings = How your Bible translates it
cite-option-occurrences = Where it appears
cite-option-family = Word family
cite-option-reading = Pronunciation of each word
cite-option-gloss = Meaning of each word
cite-option-translation = Verse in your Bible
# $word: the word in the original; $place: the verse.
cite-word-chip = { $word } ({ $place })
# $language: "Greek" or "Hebrew".
cite-original-chip = { $place } in { $language }
cite-word-source = { $place }, { $language }
cite-term-source = { $lemma }, { $language } dictionary. STEPBible (CC BY 4.0)
cite-interlinear-source = { $place }, { $language }. STEPBible (CC BY 4.0)
cite-from-lemma = from { $lemma }
cite-heading-also = Also
cite-renders-in = How { $bible } translates it
cite-family = Family
cite-language-greek = Greek
cite-language-hebrew = Hebrew
# Words that, after a passage ("Mt 5:3 greek"), ask for the original text; comma separated.
cite-search-keywords = original,greek,hebrew,griego,hebreo
cite-term-hit = { $lemma } ({ $translit })
cite-term-hit-snippet = Dictionary: { $gloss }. { $count ->
    [one] 1 time
   *[other] { $count } times
}
cite-interlinear-snippet = Word by word: original, pronunciation and meaning
cite-needs-originals = The original languages are not on this device.
